{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"builder pattern builder pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","fileName":"Builder Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Builder Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"builder pattern builder pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","fileName":"Builder Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Builder Pattern","heading":"Builder Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The builder pattern separates the construction process for a complex object from the finished object's representation. A builder can collect or sequence required parts, validate that construction is complete, and then produce the object. This is useful when a constructor with many optional arguments obscures which combinations are valid, but it adds little when an object can be created clearly in one step.\n\nA builder moves the steps required to assemble a complex object out of the client. Different builders can follow the same construction process while producing different representations, and a director can coordinate the sequence when that sequence itself is reusable.\n\nThe room-construction example separates a configured building process from the client that requests a completed representation. .NET Generic Host applies the same pattern by accumulating service, configuration, and logging choices before building the host.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"builder pattern builder pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Builder Pattern.md","fileName":"Builder Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Builder Pattern","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}